UNIT_ID: U-008
NAME: Expected Utility Thresholds for Agent Action and Dialog
LENS: LENS_SYSTEM
TYPE: algorithm
STATUS: SOURCE_SUPPORTED
FUNCTION: Decyzja o autonomii agenta oparta na expected utility: porównanie eu(A|E) i eu(¬A|E) wyznacza threshold probability p*; powyżej p* action, poniżej inaction; dialog jako trzecia opcja z własnymi thresholdami (p*¬A,D i p*D,A).
MINIMAL_FORM:
  - compute p(G|E) z observables (np. text classification)
  - assign utilities: u(A,G), u(A,¬G), u(¬A,G), u(¬A,¬G)
  - compute eu(A|E) = p(G|E)u(A,G) + [1-p(G|E)]u(A,¬G)
  - compute eu(¬A|E) = p(G|E)u(¬A,G) + [1-p(¬G|E)]u(¬A,¬G)
  - threshold p* where eu(A|E) = eu(¬A|E); action if p(G|E) > p*
  - extend to dialog: u(D,G), u(D,¬G); thresholds p*¬A,D (inaction→dialog) i p*D,A (dialog→action)
SOURCE_ANCHOR:
  - source: Principles of Mixed-Initiative User Interfaces
    locator: erichorvitz.com/chi99horvitz.pdf
    anchor: §FROM BELIEFS TO ACTIONS (Equations 1–3, Fig. 4–6)
    revision: UNKNOWN
EVIDENCE_TYPE: SOURCE_FACT
EVIDENCE_LAYER: DOCUMENTED_DESIGN
EFFECT_STATUS: TESTED_IN_SOURCE
TRANSFER_FORM: ALGORITHM
LIMITS:
  - utilities mogą być context-dependent (attention, screen real estate, rush); thresholds mogą być directly assessed by designers or users zamiast explicit computation

