UNIT_ID: U-010
NAME: Five Levels of Agent Autonomy Defined by User Role
LENS: LENS_SYSTEM
TYPE: design_principle
STATUS: SOURCE_SUPPORTED
FUNCTION: Framework pięciu poziomów autonomii agenta, zdefiniowanych przez rolę użytkownika: L1 operator (user-managed planning, invocation/approval before actions), L2 collaborator (shared planning, control transfer, shared representation), L3 consultant (agent plans, consults user for expertise/preferences), L4 approver (agent requests involvement only for blockers/high-risk actions), L5 observer (full autonomy, monitoring + emergency off-switch).
MINIMAL_FORM:
  - L1: user performs high-level planning; agent requires invocation or approval before actions; avoids preference-based decision-making
  - L2: user and agent collaboratively plan, delegate, execute; user can modify agent's work and take control anytime
  - L3: agent plans and executes most tasks; user consulted for expertise/preferences; user can request changes but not directly take control
  - L4: agent requests user involvement only when reaching failure or high-risk state; user may specify conditions for seeking approval
  - L5: agent plans and executes all tasks; user can monitor via activity logs; only control is emergency off-switch
